traceability.evidence:
Story: docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md

CORE PLUGIN STRUCTURE & RULE REGISTRY (REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE, REQ-RULE-REGISTRY, REQ-NPM-PACKAGE):
- src/index.ts defines a standard ESLint plugin object and exports it:
  - RULE_NAMES enumerates rule modules:
    ["require-story-annotation","require-req-annotation","require-branch-annotation","valid-annotation-format","valid-story-reference","valid-req-reference","prefer-implements-annotation"]
  - Dynamic rule loading with graceful fallback:
    ```ts
    const rules: Record = {} as any;
    RULE_NAMES.forEach((name) => {
      try {
        const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`);
        rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod;
      } catch (error: any) {
        console.error(`[eslint-plugin-traceability] Failed to load rule "${name}": ${error.message}`);
        rules[name] = {
          meta: { type: "problem", docs: { description: `Failed to load rule '${name}'` }, schema: [] },
          create(context: Rule.RuleContext) {
            return {
              Program(node: any) {
                context.report({
                  node,
                  message: `eslint-plugin-traceability: Error loading rule "${name}": ${error.message}`,
                });
              },
            };
          },
        } as Rule.RuleModule;
      }
    });
    const plugin = { rules };
    export { rules, configs, maintenance };
    export default plugin;
    ```
- Package is a valid npm plugin package (package.json):
  - "name": "eslint-plugin-traceability"
  - "main": "lib/src/index.js", "types": "lib/src/index.d.ts"
  - "files": ["lib","README.md","LICENSE","SECURITY.md","user-docs","CHANGELOG.md"]
  - peerDependencies: { "eslint": "^9.0.0" }
  - TypeScript tooling present: devDependencies include "typescript", "ts-jest", "@types/jest" and build scripts ("build": "tsc -p tsconfig.json", "type-check": "tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json").
- Tests explicitly verifying plugin exports and rule registry:
  - tests/plugin-setup.test.ts:
    ```ts
    import plugin, { rules, configs } from "../src/index";
    it("[REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE] plugin exports rules and configs", () => {
      expect(rules).toBeDefined();
      expect(configs).toBeDefined();
      expect(typeof rules).toBe("object");
      expect(typeof configs).toBe("object");
      expect(plugin.rules).toBe(rules);
      expect(plugin.configs).toBe(configs);
    });
    ```
  - tests/plugin-default-export-and-configs.test.ts asserts that rules keys equal the expected list and that configs are wired to those rules.
- Jest run (command: `npm test -- --verbose`) shows:
  - PASS tests/plugin-setup.test.ts — "Traceability ESLint Plugin (Story 001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP) ✓ [REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE] plugin exports rules and configs".

CONFIG SYSTEM & ESLINT v9 FLAT CONFIG INTEGRATION (REQ-ESLINT-COMPAT, REQ-CONFIG-SYSTEM, REQ-RULE-REGISTRY):
- src/index.ts defines flat-config presets:
  ```ts
  const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES = {
    "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/require-req-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/require-branch-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/valid-annotation-format": "warn",
    "traceability/valid-story-reference": "error",
    "traceability/valid-req-reference": "error",
    "traceability/prefer-implements-annotation": "warn",
  } as const;
  function createTraceabilityFlatConfig() {
    return { rules: { ...TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES } };
  }
  const configs = {
    recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
    strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
  };
  plugin.configs = configs;
  ```
- ESLint v9 flat config usage is tested via FlatESLint:
  - tests/config/flat-config-presets-integration.test.ts:
    ```ts
    import { FlatESLint } from "eslint/use-at-your-own-risk";
    import { configs, default as traceabilityPlugin } from "../../src/index";
    const baseConfig = { plugins: { traceability: traceabilityPlugin }, rules: {} };
    const config = [baseConfig, ...configs.recommended];
    const eslint = new FlatESLint({ overrideConfig: config, overrideConfigFile: true, ignore: false });
    const [result] = await eslint.lintText("function foo() {}", { filePath: "example.js" });
    const ruleIds = result.messages.map((m) => m.ruleId).sort();
    expect(ruleIds).toContain("traceability/require-story-annotation");
    ```
- Jest output shows this integration passing:
  - "Flat config presets integration (Story 002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG) ✓ [REQ-CONFIG-PRESETS] recommended preset enables traceability rules via documented usage" and similar for strict preset.
- Project-level eslint.config.js is itself a flat config that loads the plugin (source or built) and wires it into TS/JS files via `plugins: { traceability: plugin }`.

CLI / ESLINT INTEGRATION & CORE FUNCTIONALITY (Core Functionality, REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE, REQ-ESLINT-COMPAT):
- End-to-end ESLint CLI integration test:
  - tests/integration/cli-integration.test.ts:
    ```ts
    const eslintPkgDir = path.dirname(require.resolve("eslint/package.json"));
    const eslintCliPath = path.join(eslintPkgDir, "bin", "eslint.js");
    const configPath = path.resolve(__dirname, "../../eslint.config.js");
    function runEslint(code: string, rule: string) {
      const args = [
        "--no-config-lookup",
        "--config", configPath,
        "--stdin",
        "--stdin-filename", "foo.js",
        "--rule", "no-unused-vars:off",
        "--rule", rule,
      ];
      return spawnSync(process.execPath, [eslintCliPath, ...args], { encoding: "utf-8", input: code });
    }
    it.each(tests)("[REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE] $name", ({ code, rule, expectedStatus }) => {
      const result = runEslint(code, rule);
      expect(result.status).toBe(expectedStatus);
    });
    ```
- Scenarios include missing @story, present @story, missing @req, and invalid/path-traversal annotations, confirming that rules register and execute via the real ESLint CLI.
- Jest output shows this suite passing:
  - "[docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md] CLI Integration (traceability plugin)" with 5 passing test cases.

ERROR HANDLING (REQ-ERROR-HANDLING, acceptance criterion already [x]):
- src/index.ts wraps rule loading in try/catch, logs the error, and installs a placeholder rule that reports a diagnostic:
  ```ts
  try {
    const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`);
    rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod;
  } catch (error: any) {
    console.error(`[eslint-plugin-traceability] Failed to load rule "${name}": ${error.message}`);
    rules[name] = { /* placeholder rule that reports error in Program */ };
  }
  ```
- tests/plugin-setup-error.test.ts:
  - Mocks ../src/rules/require-branch-annotation to throw `Error("Test load error")`.
  - Requires ../src/index and asserts:
    - console.error called with `Failed to load rule "require-branch-annotation": Test load error`.
    - Placeholder rule exists with `meta.docs.description` mentioning the failure.
    - Placeholder rule's visitor reports an error message containing `Error loading rule "require-branch-annotation": Test load error`.
- Jest output shows:
  - "Traceability ESLint Plugin Error Handling (Story 001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP) ✓ [REQ-ERROR-HANDLING] should report error loading rule and provide placeholder rule".
- tests/cli-error-handling.test.ts also validates CLI-level error handling when the rule module is missing; this suite passes in the Jest run.

